    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36169" root="قمأ" body-key="q">
    
      5 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تقمّأَ المَكَانَ</span></b>  (in the CK <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المكانُ</span>) [<i>He found
that</i>] <i>the place suited him, and consequently he
abode in it.</i> (O, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تقمّأ الشَّىْءِ</span> <i>He took the
best of the thing.</i> (Th, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <i>He collected
the thing little by little:</i> (S, O:) and accord. to
Z, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الشَّىْءِ</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اقتمأ</span></b>  signifies <i>He collected the thing.</i>
(TA.)

